  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting and empowering victims in Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2009 the Social Department of the Bishops Conference (SNPS), CAFOD and the local government of Bogot&#xe1; presented a two year project to the EC Non State Actors budget line for EUR 972,000 which was approved. The main objective of the project is to strengthen the role of victims of the armed conflict and other types of victims in the Departments of Cundinamarca and Tolima in Colombia as part of peace building process. The project will involve: 
- Regional conflict analysis&apos;
- Training communities on peace building techniques and developing community action plans
- Promoting citizen participation and strengthening victims organisations
- Advocacy work on human rights and employment issues (job opportunities for victims of armed conflict) and the setting up of oversight communities to monitor public policy
- Supporting small businesses / income generating activities and creating links with businesses to provide job opportunities for victims of the armed conflict.

SNPS is the lead organisation and CAFOD is a partner therefore the EC funds will be sent to SNPS.</narrative>
  </description>
